<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Ablation value-wise Global Transition Scores (%) for entropy neurons ablation. The ablation values are computed over the knowledge probing dataset for each neuron activation distribution <math id="A6.T6.m70" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as illustrated in Figure <a href="#A6.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix F 𝐖_U’s Effective Null Space ‣ Context Copying Modulation: The Role of Entropy Neurons in Managing Parametric and Contextual Knowledge Conflicts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. Specifically they consist of: the mean <math id="A6.T6.m71" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the mode Mode<math id="A6.T6.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the median Median<math id="A6.T6.m73" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and two extreme values min(<math id="A6.T6.m74" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n_{i}}+3\sigma_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n_{i}}+3\sigma_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.T6.m75" class="ltx_Math" alttext="max_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">max_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>), max(<math id="A6.T6.m76" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n_{i}}-3\sigma_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n_{i}}-3\sigma_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.T6.m77" class="ltx_Math" alttext="min_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">min_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>) where <math id="A6.T6.m78" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard deviation. For the extreme values, we make sure to take the min<math id="A6.T6.m79" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>/max<math id="A6.T6.m80" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A6.T6.m81" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n_{i}}\pm 3\sigma_{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n_{i}}\pm 3\sigma_{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is out of distribution.</figcaption>
</figure>
